{
  "_id": "fhSubEmbergrss01",
  "name": "Embergrass",
  "type": "consumable",
  "img": "icons/svg/item-bag.svg",
  "folder": "fhSubModern00001",
  "system": {
    "description": {
      "value": "<p>A loose-leaf cure of red-veined herb, rolled and smoked. Steadies the nerves and dulls the edge of a long day; chronic users complain that the days stop having edges at all.</p><p><strong><em>Desired effects on use.</em></strong> For 1 hour you have advantage on saving throws against being Frightened, and a +1 bonus to Charisma (Persuasion) checks.</p><p><strong><em>On use, save against addiction.</em></strong> Make a DC 12 Wisdom saving throw. On a failed save, you gain the Addicted condition from Embergrass (see below).</p><p><strong><em>Addicted from Embergrass.</em></strong> While you have this Addicted condition, you are also Poisoned and have disadvantage on Intelligence checks.</p><p><strong><em>Withdrawal.</em></strong> At the end of each Long Rest while addicted, you either take another dose or abstain. If you abstain, make a DC 11 Wisdom check to resist the craving; on a failure, you give in and take a dose. On a success, you go into withdrawal for 4 days, or half that if you succeed on a DC 12 Constitution saving throw. If you have no doses left, skip the Wisdom check. While in withdrawal you have disadvantage on Wisdom and Intelligence saving throws, and in combat you take 1d4 psychic damage at the start of each of your turns. Abstaining then takes only the Wisdom check, and taking any dose ends the withdrawal but not the addiction. When the withdrawal ends, so does the addiction.</p><p><strong><em>Overdose.</em></strong> If you take a dose while still under its effects, or once your tolerance is at its limit, there is a 10% chance you overdose: you take 2d6 psychic damage and have the Incapacitated condition for 1 round.</p><p><strong><em>Dosing others.</em></strong> As an action, you can blow a dose into the face of a creature within 5 feet. It must succeed on a DC 12 Constitution saving throw or be dosed.</p><p><em>Requires ready paraphernalia that applies to inhaled substances, such as Rolling Papers or a Calibrated Inhaler.</em></p>"
    },
